  "notes": "UK entertainer-pop, modelled on the straight-time half of the catalogue: the research splits 75–96 ballads (half-time, backbeat on 3) from 103–130 uptempos (straight), and since the sourced single is the sampled-funk one the session takes the 103–130 band with `halfTime` false. The ballad band is named here rather than encoded; the parent's inherited ballad mood covers the slow end. Drums are the entry's two-layer claim — \"live kit tracked loose plus a programmed loop underneath\" — so this is one of the few models in the section that opens up `humanize`: the quantize strength drops to 0.78 with real timing jitter on every lane. The sampled disco break gives the three deltas: kick 1/3, \"16th hat with an open hat on 4&\", and the \"marching 8th snare and a huge crash pattern\" of the anthems, which is the crash/tambourine perc block and a ladder on the snare roll. Harmony is I–V–vi–IV for the anthems and I–IV with a blues-flattened 7th for the funk material, hence mixolydian in the scale weights. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research rates it high-medium and says the key/progression detail is inferred. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are all drum probabilities, the humanize values and `bpm.mode` 112.",
